  "description": "BUSLAE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C134 H163 Dy5 O21 S12,3(C3 H6 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.571-5.480 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.06-179.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(μ5-OH)(μ3-OH)4(L1)(L2)2(acac)2(CH3OH)2]·3acetone·2CH3OH (H3L2 = 5,11,17,23-tetrakis(1,1-dimethylethyl)-25,26,27-trihydroxy-28-methoxythiacalix[4]arene); empirical C145H189Dy5O26S12. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ5-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ5-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
